Art Willis <nhplayer@trantor.nospam.com> writes:
> One final point, art1-343.txt says that Magicbane can be
> randomly generated, but David Leon <dzleon@yahoo.com> says
> in a previous post, that it can't be since athames are not
> randomly generated.

Careful here. The _artifact_ can be randomly generated in place of a
regular item; that regular item itself need not have been randomly
generated in the NetHackish sense :-)

> I believe that (some) lichs can be created with athames, so is it
> the case that one of them could be generated with Magicbane, but
> that it would never occur as a death drop?

Exactly so. If an athame _is_ generated, under circumstances in which
it is not specifically debarred from becoming an artifact, then it has
a 1/20 chance of being made Magicbane. This currently only applies to
arch-liches' 2/9 chance of being issued one, and only 1/13 of the time
then (for an overall chance per arch-lich of 1/1170). The other 12/13
of the time, and all of master liches' 6/7 chance of getting one, it's
specifically debarred as above.

Furthermore, wizard player-monsters also have a 3/8 chance of being
issued an athame; whether on the Astral Plane or not, this is also
specifically debarred, but on the Astral Plane the 50% chance,
mentioned later in that paragraph of art1-343.txt, then kicks in.

